<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>Somoni 0.8.0</title>
    <style>
        body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 52rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 1rem; line-height: 1.5; }
        nav a { margin-right: 1rem; }
        pre { background: #f4f4f4; padding: 1rem; overflow-x: auto; }
        @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
            body { background: #1b1b1b; color: #eee; }
            pre { background: #2a2a2a; }
            a { color: #8ab4f8; }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <header>
        <h1>Somoni</h1>
        <p>Version 0.8.0, built with Somoni itself</p>
        <nav>
            <a href="#start">What is Somoni?</a>
            <a href="#typen">Variables and types</a>
            <a href="#funktionen">Functions and lambdas</a>
            <a href="#klassen">Classes and interfaces</a>
            <a href="#module">Module</a>
            <a href="#templates">Templates</a>
        </nav>
    </header>
    <main>
<section id="start">
    <h2>What is Somoni?</h2>
    <p>Somoni is a strongly typed language with curly braces. A type checker finds errors before the program runs, a VM runs the bytecode.</p>
    <pre><code>print(&quot;Hello Somoni&quot;);

var name = &quot;Ali&quot;;
print(&quot;Hello {name}!&quot;);</code></pre>
    <ul>
        <li>Run a program: somoni file.smn</li>
        <li>Named after Ismoil Somoni</li>
        <li>Interpreter written in Rust: lexer, parser, type checker, compiler, VM</li>
    </ul>
</section>
<section id="typen">
    <h2>Variables and types</h2>
    <p>Every variable has a fixed type. It may be left out, then it is the type of the value.</p>
    <pre><code>var count = 0;              // int
const pi: float = 3.14;
var names = [&quot;Ali&quot;, &quot;Bea&quot;];    // list&lt;string&gt;
var ages = {&quot;Ali&quot;: 30};       // map&lt;string, int&gt;
var found: int? = null;       // int or null

if (found != null) {
    print(found + 1);
}</code></pre>
    <ul>
        <li>int, float, bool, string, list, map, tuple, struct, enum, result</li>
        <li>No silent conversion: &quot;5&quot; + 1 is an error</li>
        <li>A value with ? must be checked for null before it is used</li>
    </ul>
</section>
<section id="funktionen">
    <h2>Functions and lambdas</h2>
    <p>Functions have types for their parameters and their result. Lambdas may leave them out where they are known.</p>
    <pre><code>fn square(x: int): int {
    return x * x;
}

var users = [User { name: &quot;Ali&quot;, age: 30 }];
print(users.map(fn(u) =&gt; u.name));
print(users.filter(fn(u) =&gt; u.age &gt; 18));</code></pre>
    <ul>
        <li>map, filter, reduce, any, all and sort_by give the lambda its types</li>
        <li>Lambdas copy the outside variables they use</li>
    </ul>
</section>
<section id="klassen">
    <h2>Classes and interfaces</h2>
    <p>Classes with a constructor, visibility, inheritance and interfaces.</p>
    <pre><code>interface Shape {
    area(): float;
}

class Circle implements Shape {
    private r: float;

    constructor(r: float) {
        this.r = r;
    }

    area(): float {
        return 3.14 * this.r * this.r;
    }
}</code></pre>
    <ul>
        <li>public, private, protected, readonly, static, abstract</li>
        <li>extends and super, override is checked</li>
        <li>instanceof narrows the type</li>
    </ul>
</section>
<section id="module">
    <h2>Module</h2>
    <p>A file marks what it shares with export. Other files get it with import.</p>
    <pre><code>import { square } from &quot;math.smn&quot;;
import * as text from &quot;text.smn&quot;;

print(square(4));</code></pre>
    <ul>
        <li>export before fn, struct, enum, class, interface or const</li>
        <li>Every file is read once, import cycles are reported</li>
    </ul>
</section>
<section id="templates">
    <h2>Templates</h2>
    <p>Files name.template.smn are HTML with values and directives. This page is built that way.</p>
    <pre><code>@props(title: string, pages: list&lt;Page&gt;)
&lt;h1&gt;{{ title }}&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
@foreach (page: Page in pages)
    &lt;li&gt;{{ page.title }}&lt;/li&gt;
@endforeach
&lt;/ul&gt;</code></pre>
    <ul>
        <li>{{ }} always escapes, {!! !!} writes raw HTML</li>
        <li>@if, @elseif, @else, @foreach, @include</li>
        <li>A typo in a template is an error before the program runs, with file and line</li>
    </ul>
</section>
    </main>
</body>
</html>
